# Frontend Design QA Plugin Package Boundary

Use this Rule when writing or reviewing reusable Frontend Design QA plugin content.

The plugin package must be self-contained for consumers who only receive the `frontend-design-qa` plugin folder. A required Section or CPT frontend QA step must not depend on files elsewhere in this development repository.

## Required Checks

- Every required Skill, Rule, reference, script, checklist, validator, or workflow contract named by the plugin must exist inside the plugin package, which is `plugins/frontend-design-qa` in this development repository, or be explicitly marked as an optional external dependency.
- Default Frontend Design QA workflows must not require `.agents`, `.cursor/plugins/cache`, `weseo-smartflow-frontend-guide`, `.scratch`, repository-local scripts, or any other development-only path.
- If a workflow says "run `<skill-name>`", that Skill must be bundled in `plugins/frontend-design-qa/skills/<skill-name>/SKILL.md` unless the workflow clearly says the Skill is optional and external.
- `PROJECT-CONTEXT.md` is a project-local file in the current project workspace. Do not reference a plugin-local Project Context template unless this package actually bundles that file.
- Section and CPT handoff templates are owned by WST Builder. Filled handoffs live at project-configured storage locations from Project Context, not inside reusable plugin package folders.
- Project-local validators, project-local Playwright test commands, build commands, test locations, browser URLs, theme tokens, selectors, and WP Grid Builder IDs must be described as project-local unless they are bundled with the current project.
- The Playwright MCP server configuration lives only in the untracked `.cursor/mcp.json` of the local Cursor workspace. Reusable plugin guidance may show placeholder shapes with `<playwright-mcp-package>` but must not embed a hard-coded package name, version, or credential.
- Reusable guidance must not include real client IDs, server paths, URLs, ACF keys, field post IDs, WP Grid Builder IDs, credentials, token-bearing examples, repository names, theme tokens, Figma file URLs, build commands, Playwright commands, deployment steps, or project-only values.
- The plugin README, manifest, release notes, rules, and skills must agree on the bundled content list.
- Manifest `source` fields and archive references are development provenance only. Runtime `path` fields and required workflow references must point to bundled plugin content.

Stop and fix the package before shipping if a required workflow path points outside the plugin folder without being marked optional or project-local, or if reusable guidance contains project-only values.
